{
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "heading", "text": "What is a Hybrid Quantum Neural Network?", "level": 2 },
    { "type": "text", "body": "A **Hybrid Neural Network** places a parameterized quantum circuit as a intermediate layer inside a classical neural network pipeline. Classical linear layers reduce high-dimensional inputs (e.g. 784-pixel images) down to 2–4 bottleneck features, which feed into the quantum layer." },
    { "type": "callout", "variant": "info", "body": "To train hybrid networks end-to-end, backpropagation requires calculating gradients through quantum circuits. This is accomplished using the Parameter-Shift Rule." },

    { "type": "heading", "text": "The Parameter-Shift Rule", "level": 2 },
    { "type": "text", "body": "Unlike classical code where automatic differentiation evaluates exact derivative formulas, quantum circuits compute analytic gradients by evaluating the circuit at two shifted parameter values:" },
    { "type": "math", "latex": "\\frac{\\partial \\langle Z(\\theta) \\rangle}{\\partial \\theta_i} = \\frac{\\langle Z(\\theta_i + \\frac{\\pi}{2}) \\rangle - \\langle Z(\\theta_i - \\frac{\\pi}{2}) \\rangle}{2}", "display": true },

    { "type": "heading", "text": "Hybrid Quantum Layer Circuit", "level": 2 },
    { "type": "step_circuit", "numQubits": 2, "caption": "Quantum Bottleneck Layer: Pre-processed inputs (x_0, x_1) + Trainable weights (θ_0, θ_1)",
      "gates": [
        { "id": "hnn1", "gate": "RY", "qubits": [0], "column": 0, "param": 0.785 },
        { "id": "hnn2", "gate": "RY", "qubits": [1], "column": 0, "param": 1.57 },
        { "id": "hnn3", "gate": "CX", "qubits": [0, 1], "column": 1 },
        { "id": "hnn4", "gate": "RZ", "qubits": [0], "column": 2, "param": 0.42 },
        { "id": "hnn5", "gate": "RZ", "qubits": [1], "column": 2, "param": -0.91 }
      ],
      "stepDescriptions": [
        "Classical Linear Layer output (x_0, x_1) enters quantum layer",
        "Ry rotation encodes classical hidden activation into qubits",
        "Entangling CNOT layer captures cross-feature quantum correlations",
        "Trainable Rz weights θ updated via Parameter-Shift Rule backpropagation"
      ]
    },

